"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[526],{5078(e,t,o){o.r(t),o.d(t,{_pageData:()=>i,default:()=>a});var n=o(641);const i=JSON.parse('{"path":"/bagisto-connector/connection-setup.html","title":"Connection Setup","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"prev":"/bagisto-connector/installation.md"},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"bagisto-connector/connection-setup.md"}'),s={name:"connection-setup.md"},a=(0,o(6262).A)(s,[["render",function(e,t,o,i,s,a){return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="connection-setup" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#connection-setup"><span>Connection Setup</span></a></h1><p>To begin synchronizing data between WooCommerce and Bagisto, you must first establish a secure connection between the two systems.</p><hr><h2 id="obtaining-bagisto-api-credentials" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#obtaining-bagisto-api-credentials"><span>Obtaining Bagisto API Credentials</span></a></h2><p>Before configuring the plugin in WooCommerce, you need to generate an API token from your Bagisto admin panel:</p><ol><li>Log in to your <strong>Bagisto Admin Panel</strong>.</li><li>Navigate to <strong>Integration</strong> &gt; <strong>Tokens</strong>.</li></ol><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/integration.png" alt="Integration Listing"></p><ol start="3"><li><p>Click the <strong>Create Integration</strong> button.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/create-integration.png" alt="Create Integration"></p></li><li><p>Fill in the required integration details:</p><ul><li>Name</li><li>Description (optional)</li><li>Assign User</li><li>Permission Type (All or Custom)</li><li>If Custom is selected, choose the required permissions from the Access Control section.</li></ul></li><li><p>Click <strong>Save</strong> to create the integration.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/access-contorl.png" alt="Access Control Settings"></p></li><li><p>In the Token Settings section, configure the token options such as:</p><ul><li>Validity (Never Expires or Expiry Date)</li><li>Rate Limit (Per Minute)</li><li>Rate Limit (Per Day)</li><li>IP Allowlist (Optional)</li></ul><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/token-setting.png" alt="Token Settings"></p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Generate Token</strong>. A confirmation dialog will appear informing you that the plaintext token will be shown only once.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/generate-token-pop-up.png" alt="Generate Token Pop-up"></p></li><li><p>Click <strong>Agree</strong> to generate the access token.</p></li><li><p>Copy the generated API token immediately, as it will not be displayed again after leaving the page.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/token-genrated-successfully.png" alt="Generated Token Successfully"></p></li><li><p>Keep the following information safe for future API authentication:</p><ul><li><strong>Bagisto Site URL</strong></li><li><strong>Generated API Token</strong></li></ul></li></ol><hr><h2 id="connecting-woocommerce-to-bagisto" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#connecting-woocommerce-to-bagisto"><span>Connecting WooCommerce to Bagisto</span></a></h2><p>Once you have the API credentials, follow these steps in your WooCommerce dashboard:</p><ol><li>Navigate to <strong>WC to Bagisto</strong> &gt; <strong>Connection</strong> in the WordPress sidebar.</li><li>You will see the Connection Settings page where you must provide your Bagisto details.</li></ol><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/connect-woocommerce-with-bagisto.png" alt="Connection Settings"></p><h3 id="configuration-fields" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#configuration-fields"><span>Configuration Fields</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Bagisto Site URL:</strong> Enter the base URL of your Bagisto storefront (e.g., <code>https://your-bagisto-store.com</code>). Ensure it starts with <code>http://</code> or <code>https://</code> and does not include a trailing slash.</li><li><strong>Bagisto API Token:</strong> Paste the API token you generated from the Bagisto admin panel.</li><li><strong>Test Connection:</strong> Before saving, it is highly recommended to click the <strong>Test Connection</strong> button to verify that WooCommerce can communicate with Bagisto using the provided credentials.</li></ul><h3 id="saving-the-connection" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#saving-the-connection"><span>Saving the Connection</span></a></h3><p>After a successful test, click the <strong>Save Connection</strong> button. The plugin will securely store your credentials and unlock the other configuration menus such as Settings, Bulk Sync, and Logs.</p><blockquote><p>[!NOTE] If the connection fails, verify that your Bagisto URL is correct, the API token is active, and there are no firewall or server restrictions blocking requests from your WordPress server.</p></blockquote>',18)])])}]])}}]);